          %title Selected writings
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 20px 10px 20px;"}
            %img{:alt => "Graeme Segal in Berkely, 1982", :src => "http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Graeme_Segal.jpeg/225px-Graeme_Segal.jpeg", :width => "250"}/
            %br/
            %p
              %a{:href => "http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Graeme_Segal.jpeg"}> Wikimedia Commons image
              , taken by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Bergman"} George Bergman
            %p in 1982
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ox.ac.uk/people/graeme.segal"} institute page
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graeme_Segal"} Wikipedia entry
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathgenealogy.org/id.php?id=27142"} MathGenealogy page
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequences"} spectral sequences
            (and introducing, following
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "Segal+condition#Grothendieck61"} Grothendicek 61
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Segal+space"} complete
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+space"} Segal space
          %ul
            %li#Segal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classifying spaces and spectral sequences
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+rings"} representation rings
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
          %ul
            %li#Segal68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The representation ring of a compact Lie group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=PMIHES_1968__34__113_0"} numdam:PMIHES_1968__34__113_0
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %ul
            %li#Segal68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant K-theory
              %strong 34
              (1968) 129-151 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/PMIHES_1968__34__129_0"}> numdam:PMIHES_1968__34__129_0
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Segal+completion+theorem"} Atiyah-Segal completion theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Equivariant
                  = succeed "-theory" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %strong 3
              1-2 (1969) 1-18 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214428815"}> euclid:jdg/1214428815
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            and the isomorphism between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+Cohomotopy"} equivariant stable Cohomotopy
            of the point:
          %ul
            %li#Segal71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SegalEquivariantStableHomotopyTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
            from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+loop+spaces"} iterated loop spaces
          %ul
            %li#Segal73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Configuration-spaces and iterated loop-spaces
              %strong 21
              (1973), 213–221. MR 0331377 (
              %a{:href => "http://dodo.pdmi.ras.ru/~topology/books/segal.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kahn-Priddy+theorem"} Kahn-Priddy theorem
            (and a pre-cursor of
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snaith%27s+theorem"} Snaith's theorem
          %ul
            %li#Segal73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The stable homotopy of complex of projective space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Segal72.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/qmath/24.1.1"} doi:10.1093/qmath/24.1.1
          %p
            On
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+permutative+categories"} K-theory of permutative categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gamma+spaces"} Gamma spaces
            as models for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectra"} connective spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Cohomotopy"} stable Cohomotopy
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
          %ul
            %li#Segal74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories and cohomology theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(74)90022-6"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(74)90022-6
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/SegalCategoriesAndCohomologyTheories.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion+theorem"} group completion theorem
          %ul
            %li#McDuffSegal76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dusa+McDuff"}> Dusa McDuff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homology fibrations and the “group-completion” theorem
              %strong 31
              3 (1976) 279-284 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01403148"}> doi:10.1007/BF01403148
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            motivated by equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+loop+spaces"} iterated loop spaces
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+spaces+of+points"} configuration spaces of points
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              %em Some results in equivariant homotopy theory
              (1978) &amp;lbrack;scan:
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://homepages.warwick.ac.uk/~maaac/segal.html"} web
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Segal-EquivariantHT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Proving the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
          %ul
            %li#JamesSegal78
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+James"}> Ioan James
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
              = succeed "," do
                %em On equivariant homotopy type
              %strong 17
              3 (1978) 267-272 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(78)90030-7"}> doi:10.1016/0040-9383(78)90030-7
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+of+spaces+of+rational+functions"} homotopy type of spaces of rational functions
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            to itself (related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            and to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"} configuration space of points
            in
